  /* ---------------- Claire: the long way up ----------------
     Everything she has ever done with him happened indoors and on a
     clock: a stockroom, a car, a restaurant she braced in, his room, her
     room above a chemist. All of it enclosed, all of it borrowed or
     temporary, all of it in a town she was only ever passing through.

     This one is outside, in daylight, on a hill she could see from every
     window she ever stood at and never once walked up. It is the last
     thing on an eleven-week list with one item on it. Nothing is hidden
     and nothing is on a timer and the town is down there the whole time,
     small enough to hold a hand over — which is the only way she has ever
     been able to look at it. */
