      "narrator::Claire doesn't say anything for a while. She just stands there with her hands in her coat pockets looking at three years of her life laid out small enough to cover with a hand.",
      "claire::“It's tiny,” she says eventually. “That's it. That's the whole thing. I've been suffocating in that for three years and you can see the *edges* of it.”",
