  /* ---------------- Zoe: the third act ----------------
     The Tuesday theatre group has been background from the start, on
     purpose — it explains where the skill comes from and never gets to be
     the point of a scene. This is where it becomes the point.

     Her defect is the easier version: years of handing people a Zoe that
     goes down smoothly, and she is very good at it. She has stopped doing
     it to him. She has not stopped doing it to anybody else, and the
     Tuesday hall is the one room where she never had to, because nothing
     that happens there counts.

     So the test is somebody making it count. Q6 is the letter and the
     forecast she makes about herself. Q7 is the room, where she does the
     easy one for a page and a half before she hears it — and the win is
     not that she's fearless, it's that she notices. */
