      "player::You don't ask me anything.",
      "jade::“No.”",
      "player::Why not?",
      "jade::“Because you'd tell me.” She sits down on the toolbox opposite, both hands round her own mug. “Everyone tells me. I get four weeks in a town and by week two I know who's sleeping where. It's not a talent, it's just — people talk to whoever's leaving.”",
      "narrator::She drinks. Outside and two floors down, a car goes past.",
