  /* ---------------- Jade: the return leg ----------------
     A hotel room is the one kind of room she has ever been comfortable in,
     and she worked out why on the coach: it is designed to be left. You
     are supposed to go. Nobody has ever asked a hotel room to mean
     anything, which is exactly the arrangement she has had with eleven
     towns and every bed in them.

     So the last one is in the one room that is built for leaving — and it
     is the first journey of her life with a return leg on it that isn't
     her running out of somewhere. Two nights, a print of something at the
     Roxy, and a room neither of them lives in.

     She is not a woman who does gestures. The red thing is a gesture. */
