      "narrator::The print is scratched to bits and the sound is thin and there's a splice ten minutes in that jumps, and Jade watches all hundred and six minutes of it without moving once.",
      "narrator::Afterwards she stands in the foyer looking up at the box like a woman looking at a house she grew up in.",
      "jade::“Carbon arc,” she says. “You can smell it. There's about nine people left alive who'll run one and I've just watched one of them do it badly and I've never been happier.”",
      "narrator::The hotel is four streets over and does not have a lift. She goes up ahead of you with the key, which is an actual key on an actual fob, and says she'll be two minutes, and takes eleven.",
      "narrator::You give it the eleven. Then you go in.",
      "narrator::She's stood at the end of the bed in red. Not the practical black she lives in, not something out of the bag — red, and new, and bought for this, and she has clearly been standing there for a portion of those eleven minutes deciding whether to still be standing there when the door went.",
      "narrator::Jade does not do gestures. She has never once in her life done a gesture.",
      "jade::“Don't say anything for a second,” she says. “I've got a whole thing about how this isn't like me and I need to not say it.”",
      "player::Then don't say it.",
      "jade::“I bought it in Marbury in the twenty minutes between coaches,” she says immediately. “I said I wasn't going to say it and that was four seconds. Right. Yes. I've never bought anything for a *reason* before.”",
      "narrator::She stands there and lets you look at her, which costs her something, and which she does anyway.",
      "jade::“Eleven towns,” she says. “Every one of them I've been in a room like this at some point. Travelodges, guest houses, one genuinely alarming place in Hartleigh. And it's the only kind of room I've ever slept properly in.”",
      "player::Why?",
      "jade::“Because you're *meant* to leave a hotel room.” She says it like she's been turning it over for two hours on a coach, which she has. “Nobody asks it to mean anything. You go. That's the arrangement. And I worked out somewhere around Marbury that I've been treating eleven towns like hotel rooms and it's the first time I've ever been embarrassed by something I thought of myself.”",
      "narrator::She comes over and gets your coat off you, and then takes rather longer over the rest of it than she needs to.",
      { speaker: "narrator", text: "She gets down on the carpet at the end of a hotel bed and takes you in her mouth with the red still on, unhurried, both hands on you and no method anywhere in it.", video: "jade/action4/jadeboquete1.mp4" },
      "jade::“Two nights,” she says, at one point, apparently to herself. “There's a whole day in the middle. I keep coming back to that. There's a *middle*.”"
