            "narrator::She covers her face, still laughing, and when she drops her hands she's smiling in a way you've never seen on her — completely unguarded, no counter between you, no script left.",
            "claire::“Okay. New plan. Neither of us says the thing tonight.” She holds out a hand for you to shake on it, mock-serious. “We both just — know it. And we do something about it when we're less pathetic.”",
            "narrator::You shake on it. She doesn't let go of your hand afterward, and she clearly notices, and she clearly doesn't care."
