  /* ---------------- Lily: the list ----------------
     The coast worked, and then they came home, and eight days of rota put
     it quietly back in its box. This is her refusing that.

     The spine is the one defect she named herself: she cannot ask. She can
     write, though — nine years of lists have made a woman who can put
     anything on paper and nothing into a sentence. So she puts herself on
     the list, at the bottom, under the boiler, in the same neat hand.

     Which is why the anal is the centre of this and not a stunt: it's the
     first thing she has ever asked for out loud in her life, and she still
     had to write it down first to manage it. Everything before it is her
     getting to the sentence and everything after it is what's left of her
     when she doesn't have to hold anything. */

  /* ---------------- Lily: the eight days home ----------------
     These sit between the coast and the sofa, because without them those
     two scenes are back to back and the arc loses the rhythm every other
     stretch of it has: two quests, then the scene they earned.

     Q8 fires the gun q4 loaded. She said then that the moment it went
     public it would stop being theirs and start being a thing four people
     had opinions about — so she has spent months managing that. It turns
     out nobody was waiting to have an opinion. They had simply made room,
     quietly, for weeks, without being asked, which is the one kind of help
     a woman who runs everything has never learned how to accept.

     Q9 plants the pad. The list in the next scene lands as a payoff rather
     than a device if the player has already watched her try to say it out
     loud and fail. */
  function needsLilyQuest8() {
    return !!state.flags["casual_lily_a3"] && !state.flags["lily_q8_complete"]
      && statGateMet("lily_q8_complete");
  }
  function playLilyQuest8() {
    state.flags["lily_q8_complete"] = true;
    const beats = [
      "narrator::Lily has been rehearsing since Tuesday. You can tell because the kitchen is spotless, the good mugs are out, and there is a plate of biscuits nobody asked for arranged in a fan.",
      "lily::“I'm going to tell them,” she says, without preamble, drying a hand that is already dry. “Tonight. All four at once, so it only has to happen once, and then it's done and it's public and we live with it.”",
      "player::You've made a fan of biscuits.",
      "lily::“I've made a *fan of biscuits*,” she agrees grimly. “That's how frightened I am. There's a running order. I'm not showing you the running order.”",
      "narrator::She gets them in. It takes some doing — Vivian is mid-something, Maya arrives holding a bowl of cereal at half nine at night, Noelle comes down last with her reading glasses pushed up into her hair.",
      "narrator::Lily stands with her back to the counter, in front of the biscuits, and starts item one of a running order she has clearly written down.",
      "lily::“Right. So. There's something I've been meaning to say to all of you, and I'd like to get through it without—”",
      "sabrina::“Is this about you two?”",
      "narrator::The kitchen goes very quiet. Lily's mouth stays open on a word she does not get to.",
      "maya::“Vivian.”",
      "sabrina::“What? We're all *here*. She did a fan of biscuits, Maya.”",
      "lily::“...How long have you known.”",
      "noelle::“Since the kitchen thing,” Noelle says, from the doorway, not unkindly. “Obviously.”",
      "narrator::Lily turns to Maya, who has gone extremely interested in her cereal.",
      "maya::“Okay so, in my defence, I have been running *interference* for you for weeks. Do you know how much interference? I have invented errands. I have been to a shop that isn't real.”"
    ];
    playSequenceWithReplies(beats.map(parseCasualLine), [
      { text: "Nobody's making it a thing. Look at them.", stat: "warm" },
      { text: "Then it's said. That's the whole speech done.", stat: "bold" },
      { text: "Vivian, she had a running order.", stat: "witty" }
    ], playLilyQuest8b, "sabrina::“Oh, she's *had* a running order since Sunday, I've seen it on the fridge—” and Lily makes a noise like a woman whose house has turned on her.");
  }
