  /* ---------------- Maya: the third act ----------------
     Her first two acts settled whether she'd let herself be here: no
     voices, present tense, someone in the frame. Repeating that would be
     the same quest twice.

     What's left is the other half of her, which nobody has ever asked
     about. Maya draws. She has drawn the whole house for four months in
     the margins of everything else, and treats it the way she treats
     anything that matters — as a bit, so it can fail safely. A joke that
     dies is a joke that died. A drawing that dies is just her.

     Q6 makes her say yes to a wall. Q7 puts strangers in front of it, and
     hands her the one thing her arc has never had: a reason to want a
     future here that isn't him. */
