  /* ---------------- Maya: seven months, twenty-six posters ----------------
     Her third act left a gun on the table and said so out loud: a year of
     work promised, seven months of permission to be here. These two fire
     it, and they fire it the way her arc has always worked — by making the
     abstract thing concrete and small enough to be terrifying.

     Q8 is a box on a form. Not the visa, not the money: one field marked
     OCCUPATION, which is the same question the wall asked her, in
     bureaucratic. Q9 is the other half of it, and it's the one that
     costs — she has spent five months telling her family about a boy and
     a city, and now she has to tell them she is trying not to come home.

     Deliberately not resolved. She isn't owed an answer yet. */
