  /* ---------------- Noelle: the third act ----------------
     Her first two acts were about control as armour: the framework, the
     columns, the drive with no destination she had to be talked into.
     She has already learned she can be spontaneous. Repeating that is a
     lap of the same track.

     What she has never been tested on is the sentence she said herself in
     q4 and then walked away from — I know how to be indispensable to
     people, I don't know how to be close to them. She buys safety by
     being necessary. Nobody throws away a person who is holding something
     they need.

     So q6 takes the thing she is exceptional at and makes it merely fine,
     and q7 catches her doing what she does six hours later: making herself
     necessary to somebody else instead. It ends on the question she has
     never once asked anybody in her life. */
