  /* ---------------- Noelle: four of six ----------------
     Everything up to here has been things done TO her defences: not
     organising, not being useful, being looked at, being kept for
     nothing. All of it passive. She has never once in four months said I
     want this specific thing.

     So this isn't another dismantling — she's been dismantled enough, and
     doing it again would just be the same scene louder. This is the
     opposite: she gets to be entirely herself, at full volume, and have
     that be the good outcome. She has made a list. It is numbered. It is
     in an order, and she is going to read it out one item at a time,
     because a woman who numbers things is not a woman with a defect.

     The clip order is hers, which is why the list exists: it makes the
     sequence something she chose rather than something that happened. */
